Subject: Kafka Connect and Postgres composite types
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="000000000000d9b6520640377451"

--000000000000d9b6520640377451
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Kia ora,

I had a quick search in the mailing list archive to see if this had come up
previously, apologies if it's already been covered and I missed it.

A user in the Confluent Slack hit an error with a composite type (which is
effectively a dynamic type in PG, IIRC? I never encountered them in
Postgres until today) which yielded the following error message:

> org.postgresql.util.PSQLException: ERROR: column "orchestration_details"
is of type orchestration_obj_type but expression is of type character
varying
> Hint: You will need to rewrite or cast the expression

Given that they're types that only exist in a particular DB, and there's no
(AFAICT) super-type that KC could infer them to be, I was thinking that a
potential solution might be to expose to users the ability to configure
other types that need casting in like these existing ones?

https://github.com/confluentinc/kafka-connect-jdbc/blob/master/src/main/jav=
a/io/confluent/connect/jdbc/dialect/PostgreSqlDatabaseDialect.java#L86

If this might be a viable approach, I'd like to contribute it, but it's
been a while since I've submitted a PR, would this require a KIP beforehand=
?

(Or am I even asking in the right place, given the JDBC sink is controlled
by Confluent? I'm unsure of the overlap these days)

Ng=C4=81 mihi,

Liam Clarke-Hutchinson

--000000000000d9b6520640377451--

