> Kafka Streams seems to not always release the state directory lock for al=
l tasks, when threads are added / removed.=C2=A0
> Effectively, the old thread (same name, different object) still seems to =
own the task.
> To reproduce, checkout
> [https://github.com/lucasbru/kafka/commit/2701dd39fe7df23a123939a1c9e140c=
849904b5f]
> and run `AdjustStreamThreadCountTest >=C2=A0
> shouldAddAndRemoveThreadsMultipleTimes` ... multiple times.
> =C2=A0
> The test was changed to use a stateful topology.=C2=A0
> =C2=A0
> I reproduced this on 3.9, 4.0, 4.1, trunk
> =C2=A0



