Hi Sushant,
Thanks for the KIP, overall it looks good. Some comments:

AM1: In ProposedChanges we reference "acknowledge(ConsumerRecord,
AcknowledgementType)" but the enum class is AcknowledgeType. And same at
some other places, also when we reference AcknowledgementType.RENEW.

AM2: There is a reference to UnsupportedAcknowledgementType exception but
that neither exists nor the KIP defined. Can we please add the details of
the exception in KIP as that will be public facing change.

AM3: What happens when the broker fails to Renew the acquisition lock
because of an incorrect request i.e. already expired, how does the client
send the information back to the application? Do we need to capture those
details in the KIP?

AM4: In the compatibility section, it's mentioned that "If a broker running
the old version of the code receives the *RENEW*  ack type in the request,
it should consider this an error and return the appropriate error code to
the consumer" sorry I couldn't understand this i.e. what are we proposing
by this change, we can't modify the already shipped releases?

Regards,
Apoorv Mittal


