HongYi Chen created KAFKA-19786:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Session mode compileScala reports missing classes jav=
a main directory
                 Key: KAFKA-19786
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19786
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: build
    Affects Versions: 4.1.0
            Reporter: HongYi Chen
            Assignee: HongYi Chen


*Problem*
When running `{{{}:core:compileScala{}}}` under {{{}`keepAliveMode=3DSESSIO=
N`{}}}, joint compilation adds a non-existent directory ({{{}.../core/build=
/classes/java/main{}}}) to {{{}javac{}}}=E2=80=99s classpath.
This triggers:
```
Unexpected javac output: warning: [path] bad path element ".../core/build/c=
lasses/java/main": no such file or directory
error: warnings found and -Werror specified
```
The same task succeeds under `{{{}keepAliveMode=3DDAEMON`{}}}.



*Current Workaround*
Added a scoped compiler flag `({{{}-Xlint:-path{}}})` only under `{{{}keepA=
liveMode=3DSESSION`{}}} to suppress the {{[path]}} warning and allow the bu=
ild to succeed.


*Steps to Reproduce*

```
./gradlew clean :core:compileScala -PkeepAliveMode=3Dsession =C2=A0 # fails=
 before workaround =C2=A0
./gradlew clean :core:compileScala -PkeepAliveMode=3Ddaemon =C2=A0 =C2=A0# =
succeeds =C2=A0
```

*Goal of This Ticket*
Identify why SESSION-mode joint compilation includes the missing {{classes/=
java/main}} entry in {{{}javac{}}}=E2=80=99s classpath, align its behavior =
with DAEMON mode, and remove the temporary suppression once the classpath i=
s corrected.



