> > > For clarity, let=E2=80=99s compare the three designs:
> > >  =E2=80=A2 Classic topics:
> > >    =E2=80=A2 Data and metadata are co-located in the partition log.
> > >    =E2=80=A2 The partition log content: [Batch header (metadata)|B=
atch data].
> > >    =E2=80=A2 The partition log is replicated to the followers.
> > >    =E2=80=A2 The replicas and leader have local state built from m=
etadata.
> > >  =E2=80=A2 Original Diskless:
> > >    =E2=80=A2 Metadata is in the batch coordinator, data is on remo=
te storage.
> > >    =E2=80=A2 The partition state is global in the batch coordinato=
r.
> > >  =E2=80=A2 New Diskless:
> > >    =E2=80=A2 Metadata is in the partition log, data is on remote s=
torage.
> > >    =E2=80=A2 Partition log content: [Batch header (metadata)|Batch=
 coordinates on
> > > remote storage].
> > >    =E2=80=A2 The partition log is replicated to the followers.
> > >    =E2=80=A2 The replicas and leader have local state built from m=
etadata.
