Hi Kafka Community,

I would like to call a vote for KIP-1219
<https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1219%3A+Configurations+for+KRaft+Fetch+and+FetchSnapshot+Byte+Size>.
It proposes adding two new configs which will fix a liveness problem in
KRaft.

The new configs would be:
- controller.quorum.fetch.snapshot.max.bytes
- controller.quorum.fetch.max.bytes

Relevant links:

KIP: KIP-1219
<https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1219%3A+Configurations+for+KRaft+Fetch+and+FetchSnapshot+Byte+Size>
Bug: KAFKA-19541 <https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19541>
Discussion: thread
<https://lists.apache.org/thread/sx5z18qrw5j2bmfbzgobxxycnrxngmdc>

Best,
Jonah

