Hi Chia-Ping:

Thanks for your suggestion.

1: " having`TopicBasedRemoteLogMetadataManager` extend it  "- I think it is
a good idea that we can avoid involve it into all the
RemoteLogMetadataManager even we can using default method.
the sever part can been changed to :
rlm.remoteLogMetadataManager() match {
  case callback: BrokerReadyCallback =3D>
registerBrokerReadyCallback(callback)
  case _ =3D> // RemoteLogMetadataManager doesn't implement
BrokerReadyCallback, skip registration
}

2:  making the new interface non-public
currently. It seems it isn't possible because the interface is involved in
two different package. It=E2=80=99s challenging to handle this while keepin=
g the
code elegant (any other ideas?).
So I suggest we can keep it public after all the interface method is very
simple.
org.apache.kafka.server.log.remote.metadata.storage.TopicBasedRemoteLogMeta=
dataManager;
kafka.server.BrokerServer

Thanks for your discussion!

