I love Matthias' suggestion.

> I think there's a reasonable case for decoupling this from Apache Kafka.

+1

I have forwarded this discussion to Debasish Ghosh (from the kafka-streams-sc=
ala team) for more feedback.

On 2025/10/23 23:35:01 Ismael Juma wrote:
> Thanks Matthias, this is helpful. A couple of inline comments below.
>=20
> On Thu, Oct 23, 2025 at 3:00=E2=80=AFPM Matthias J. Sax <mjsax@apache.org> =
wrote:
>=20
> > So I would say, overall there is fair usage of this module, so I am not
> > sure if we would really want to discontinue it?
> >
>=20
> Given these adoption numbers, the fact that we haven't done a particularly
> good job supporting new Scala versions and the slow rate of change for
> streams-scala (is this accurate?), I think there's a reasonable case for
> decoupling this from Apache Kafka. It would make the builds faster and
> simpler if we could remove all of the Scala machinery.
>=20
> If we really want to consider to discontinue the kafka-streams-scala
> > module, we might want to reach out to the user mailing list, too?
> >
>=20
> Makes sense.
>=20
> Thanks,
> Ismael
>=20

