Hi Ivan,

> After some evolution of the original proposal, leaderless is now limited.
We only need to be able to accept Produce requests on more than one broker
to eliminate the cross-AZ costs for producers. Do I get it right that you
propose to get rid of this? Or do I misunderstand?

Yes, that's what I meant.

About the "batch coordinator approach" VS "coordinator-less approach", I'd
like to clarify one thing: If I remember correctly, the reason we proposed
the coordinator-less approach is because we encountered some bottleneck
when designing the batch coordinator approach to support kafka queue
feature. If that's the case, I'm wondering if the "batch coordinator
approach" is still a valid option here? Or do you already have solutions to
support the kafka queue feature in batch coordinator approach?

Thank you,
Luke

