Hi Lianet,

Thanks for the new RC, I'll take time to test it this week.

I noticed you created a 4.1.1 branch. That's not part of the release
cycle, the instruction say to "Skip this section [Cut Branches] if you
are releasing a bug fix version (e.g. 2.2.1)." [0]
For bug fix releases we don't create new branches. We bump the version
in the release branch, in this case 4.1, and once a RC is voted we
create a tag, in this case 4.1.1.

0: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/Release+Process#Releas=
eProcess-CutBranches

Thanks,
Mickael

