Sanskar Jhajharia created KAFKA-19840:
-----------------------------------------

             Summary: Flaky test ShareConsumerTest. testShareGroupMaxSizeCo=
nfigExceeded
                 Key: KAFKA-19840
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19840
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
            Reporter: Sanskar Jhajharia


The test has been observed as flaky in the recent runs: [https://develocity=
.apache.org/scans/tests?search.names=3DCI%20workflow%2CGit%20repository&sea=
rch.relativeStartTime=3DP28D&search.rootProjectNames=3Dkafka&search.tags=3D=
github%2Ctrunk&search.tasks=3Dtest&search.timeZoneId=3DAsia%2FCalcutta&sear=
ch.values=3DCI%2Chttps:%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fapache%2Fkafka&tests.container=3D=
org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.ShareConsumerTest&tests.sortField=3DFLAKY=
&tests.test=3DtestShareGroupMaxSizeConfigExceeded()%5B1%5D]=C2=A0

=C2=A0
After tracing the failures, the root cause was narrowed down to commit=C2=
=A0[https://github.com/apache/kafka/commit/87657fdfc721055835f5b1f22151c461=
e85eab4a]. This change introduced a new try/catch around=C2=A0{{handleCompl=
etedAcknowledgements()}}=C2=A0in=C2=A0{{{}ShareConsumerImpl.java{}}}. The s=
ide effect is that all exceptions coming from the commit callback =E2=80=94=
 including GroupMaxSizeReachedException =E2=80=94 are now swallowed and onl=
y logged, preventing the test from ever receiving the exception.I synced wi=
th Shiv and we think that the resulting flakiness is timing dependent: * If=
 the ack callback fires while=C2=A0{{poll()}}=C2=A0is executing =E2=86=92 e=
xception is caught & swallowed =E2=86=92 test times out
 * If the callback fires outside that path =E2=86=92 exception escapes =E2=
=86=92 test passes

So the same test randomly passes/fails depending on scheduling of the ack c=
allback.



