/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-853%3A+KRaft+Controller+Membership+Changes#KI=
P853:KRaftControllerMembershipChanges-Controllerautojoining](KAFKA-19078)).=
 This is a good improvement for controller addition, but it has a minor iss=
ue, which is that when a controller is removed via removeVoterRequest, it w=
ill be added immediately due to `controller.quorum.auto.join.enable=3Dtrue`=
. In the KIP, we also mention you have to stop the controller before removi=
ng the controller:

=C2=A0
{noformat}
controller.quorum.auto.join.enable:

Controls whether a KRaft controller should automatically join the cluster=
=20
metadata partition for its cluster id. If the configuration is set to=20
true the controller must be stopped before removing the controller with kaf=
ka-metadata-quorum remove-controller.{noformat}
=C2=A0

This is not a user friendly behavior in my opinion. And it will cause many =
confusion to users and thought there is something wrong in the controller r=
emoval. Furthermore, in the kubernetes environment which is controlled by t=
he operator, it is not the cloud native way to shutdown a node, do some ope=
ration, then start it up.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

So, I propose we can improve it by "the removed controller will not be auto=
 joined before this controller restarted". That is:
1. Once the controller is removed from voters set, it won't be auto joined =
even if `controller.quorum.auto.join.enable=3Dtrue`

2. The controller can be manually join the voters in this state

3. The controller node will be auto join the voters set after node restarte=
d.

=C2=A0

So basically, the semantics is not changed, it just add some unexpected rem=
ove/add loop. Thoughts?

=C2=A0

=C2=A0



